The total number of triples from \(S'\) is \(\binom{60}{3} = 34220\). The sum \(\sum_{A \in S'} \binom{m(A)}{2}\), where \(m(A)\) is the number of points in \(S'\) lying in a closed semicircle starting at \(A\), is found by classifying points by their position and symmetry. This sum evaluates to \(28692\). Thus, the desired count is \(34220 - 28692 = 5528\).

\boxed{5528}

